<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · period</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fin de siècle</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as fin-de-siècle</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fin de siècle ('end of the century') refers to the late nineteenth and early twentieth centuries, a period associated with cultural innovation and a sense of decadence. In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a>, the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austro-Hungarian Empire</a>, it saw an extraordinary flowering in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/psychoanalysis">psychoanalysis</a>, philosophy, painting, architecture and music.</p></div>
